    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` with `@Test`) is the whole suite, and it's green. The build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event as specified.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` (in `rest/controller/v1/`):\n- An immutable `record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String primaryId, int membershipLevel)`.\n- `toJson()` renders `{\"seq\":\u2026,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"customerCode\":\u2026,\"membershipLevel\":\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` with proper JSON string escaping. The current primary identifier is carried under the `customerCode` key.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n- Added `OWNER_CREATED_SEQUENCE` (`AtomicLong`), a process-wide monotonic counter so `seq` strictly increases across all creates regardless of controller instance.\n- Extended `auditOwnerCreated(...)` to emit the structured JSON event via the `AUDIT` logger *in addition* to the existing human-readable audit line.\n- Added `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` returning `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. This is the single seam for the future evolution: when the customerCode is unified into a `memberId`, only this method changes and the event automatically carries the memberId instead \u2014 exactly matching the spec's forward-looking requirement.\n\nThe emitted line for a created owner looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\nwhich contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode \u2014 satisfying the acceptance test's `anyContains(...)` assertion.",
